From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:29:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: show locations, contact cards, events, link previews
 and media details

* Show locations, contact cards and events

These messages carry no text and were dropped. A location or the first
position of a live location is shown as a summary with a "geo:lat,lng"
URI, which the app turns into a map chip. A contact card (or several)
is written as a .vcf file into the attachment directory and shown as a
file:// link that opens the Contacts import. An event is shown as a
summary with an "event:<base64 JSON>" token the app turns into an "Add
to Calendar" chip.

* Show link previews

A message with a link preview carries a JPEG thumbnail, a title and a
description. The thumbnail is written into the attachment directory
and put, with the title and description, above the text, so the app
shows a preview card.

* Name received documents by their file name

The webOS attachment path template names files by $hash. For a
document, put its file name there, under a folder named after the
content hash, so the app's attachment chip shows the real name. The
folder keeps two different documents with the same name apart: without
it the second one overwrote the first on disk, and the first message
then showed the second file. The same document received twice still
lands in one place.

The name is reduced to characters that are safe in a path and in the
app's media URL matching; the hash alone is kept when nothing is left.

* Store a video's thumbnail as its poster

The sender's JPEG thumbnail of a video is written next to it as
<name>.jpg. The app uses it as the poster of the <video>, which the old
WebKit cannot paint from an unplayed clip.

* Deliver a picture and its caption as one message

The media link and its caption are sent as one message ("url<br>
caption") instead of two with the same id, so the app shows one bubble
with the picture and its caption.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
---
 glue/handle_attachment.c |  15 +-
 handle_attachment.go     |  44 +++++-
 handle_message.go        | 292 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 3 files changed, 340 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

